 including Ask.com, a search site with a variety of fresh and contemporary content; Reference.com that offers content across select vertical categories; Consumersearch.com, which offers content designed to simplify the product research process; and Shopping.net, a vertical shopping search site, as well as offers direct-to-consumer downloadable desktop applications. In addition, the company provides Care.com, an online destination for families to connect with caregivers for their children, aging parents, pets, and homes under the Care For Business and HomePay brands; a platform to connect healthcare professionals with job opportunities under the Vivian Health name; The Daily Beast, a website dedicated to news, commentary, culture, and entertainment that publishes original reporting and opinion; and production and producer services for feature films for sale and distribution through theatrical releases and video-on-demand services under the IAC Films name. The company was formerly known as IAC Inc. and changed its name to People Incorporated in June 2026. People Incorporated is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Neil I. Vogel | Chief Executive Officer | Age 55","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $464K ranks in the below the sector median among Communication Services peers. Each employee generates $9K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["People Incorporated is a mid-cap communication services business with a $3.3B market cap on $2.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -23% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome. Operating margins are expanding by +2.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -2% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $45M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.8\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 9.6% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 3.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.1% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Communication Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 84% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8428246013667424},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 64/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; durably derated by the market \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Advertising-cycle exposure and content/regulatory risk \u2014 a single platform policy shift or ad-spend contraction cascades through the P&L quickly.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI-generated content commoditisation \u2014 as creation costs collapse toward zero, content libraries lose pricing power and differentiation narrows.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Critical Survey: People Incorporated Common Stock (NASDAQ:PPLI) and MNTN (NYSE:MNTN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/critical-survey-people-incorporated-common-stock-nasdaqppli-and-mntn-nysemntn.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794329930.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is People (PPLI) Cheap Following Its Third Quarter Loss And Sales Drop?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nasdaq-ppli/people/news/is-people-ppli-cheap-following-its-third-quarter-loss-and-sa","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794277320.098,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Financial Comparison: People Incorporated Common Stock (NASDAQ:PPLI) versus TEN (NASDAQ:XHLD)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/financial-comparison-people-incorporated-common-stock-nasdaqppli-versus-ten-nasdaqxhld.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794201296.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.909,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How PPLI Inc (PPLI) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/How_PPLI_Inc_PPLI_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_110726091402_1794104042.html","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794104042.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"People (PPLI) Stock Looks Stretched Relative To Fair Value","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/media/nasdaq-ppli/people/news/people-ppli-stock-looks-stretched-relative-to-fair-va